-- Two phases, separated by a `synchronize`. Both write disjoint buffers and only read `A`, so
-- Bernstein accepts running all eight statements together — and `paralever autopar` would. The
-- barrier is what keeps them apart: each phase is planned on its own and the barrier survives in
-- the output. -- ref: docs/autopar.md § Synchronization

buf A[4] = arange
buf B[4]
buf C[4]

for i in 4 {
  %0 := A[i]
  B[i] := %0 * %0
}

synchronize

for i in 4 {
  %1 := A[i]
  C[i] := %1 + 1
}
